## Third-party data terms

Files in `data/` build upon three public monitoring and weather services whose provider terms apply alongside CC BY 4.0.
Downstream users must keep the source credits below.

| Provider | Package files | Required credit and provider terms |
|---|---|---|
| Water Environment Information System (WEIS), National Institute of Environmental Research, Republic of Korea (https://water.nier.go.kr) | `data/national/`, `data/national_v2/` (daily water quality, station codes and coordinates), `data/clean/geum_daily_observed.csv`, `data/clean/observed_rates.csv`, `data/clean/algae_alert_weekly.csv` | Credit: Source data from the Water Environment Information System (https://water.nier.go.kr), National Institute of Environmental Research, Republic of Korea (2025-2026). Reuse follows the public data terms of WEIS. |
| Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S) ERA5 reanalysis (Hersbach et al., 2020, *Q. J. R. Meteorol. Soc.*, 146, 1999-2049) | `data/national/era5_daily.csv`, `data/national_v2/era5_daily.csv`, `data/clean/era5_daily.csv` | Credit: Contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information 2025-2026; neither the European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use that may be made of the Copernicus information or data it contains. Reuse follows the C3S ERA5 license. |
| Open-Meteo Historical Weather API (https://open-meteo.com, `archive-api.open-meteo.com`, model `era5`) | Daily station weather series listed above | Credit: Weather data by Open-Meteo.com (https://open-meteo.com), aggregated into daily station series. Open-Meteo licenses historical weather records for non-commercial research under CC BY 4.0 (https://open-meteo.com/en/terms). |

This package omits the external GIS shapefiles for Figure 1 (HydroBASINS level-6 polygons from https://www.hydrosheds.org
and Korean river and provincial boundaries from https://www.data.go.kr). Users obtain those layers directly from their
providers under each provider's terms.
